Docker-network : What is need of creating new networks, why can't we use available n/w such as bridge network.
Ans: Because if every container is created with default n/w, then every container can communicate with each other, say front-end can communicate with DB, which would be a problem. So we create seperate n/w in such a way only required containers talk to each other.
Docker-compose : Incase of docker-compose integrated with jenkins, I used docker-compose to create 2 img and their container, but didn't link them all how we usually do in manually. But still the containers are linked. How?
Ans: Every container created will by default use bridge n/w, hence they all communicate irrespective whether we create them manually or through compose, however we are not supposed to use this default n/w cause they are more vulnerable, so always create a seperate n/w and link them.
